('112.3.b.12.A',4,'A student sees a seed. Is it living?','["no, it is a toy", "no, it is a rock", "no, it can never grow", "yes, it can grow into a plant"]'::jsonb,3,'A seed is alive and can grow into a plant.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.B',2,'A terrarium has plants, soil, and a lid. Which is nonliving?','["the soil", "a bean sprout", "a worm", "the plant"]'::jsonb,0,'Soil is a nonliving part of a terrarium.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.B',3,'In an aquarium, fish need water. What does this show?','["water is a fish", "living things depend on nonliving things", "water is alive", "fish do not need anything"]'::jsonb,1,'Fish depend on water, which is nonliving.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.B',3,'A plant in a terrarium gets light through the glass. What does the plant need the light for?','["to make shadows only", "to dig", "to make food", "to make sound"]'::jsonb,2,'Plants use light to make food.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.B',2,'Which is a living thing in an aquarium?','["a plastic castle", "water", "gravel", "a snail"]'::jsonb,3,'A snail is alive. Gravel, water, and a plastic castle are not.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.B',3,'A student sprays a terrarium with water. Why?','["the plants need water", "to make it loud", "to make it cold", "to make it smell"]'::jsonb,0,'Plants need water to live.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.B',3,'In a classroom aquarium, what happens if the water gets very dirty?','["nothing happens", "the fish can get sick", "the fish turn into plants", "the fish grow faster"]'::jsonb,1,'Living things need clean water.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.B',4,'Which pair shows a living thing depending on a nonliving thing?','["a snail and a fish", "a fish and a frog", "a fish and water", "a plant and a worm"]'::jsonb,2,'The fish needs water, a nonliving thing.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.C',2,'What do most plants use to make their own food?','["fish", "rocks", "metal", "sunlight"]'::jsonb,3,'Plants use light from the Sun to make food.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.C',3,'A rabbit eats grass. What does the rabbit get from the grass?','["food energy", "a shadow", "a magnet", "rain"]'::jsonb,0,'The rabbit gets energy from eating the grass.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.C',3,'A hawk eats a mouse and a mouse eats seeds. Which shows the food chain in order?','["mouse, hawk, seed", "seed, mouse, hawk", "hawk, mouse, seed", "seed, hawk, mouse"]'::jsonb,1,'The arrows point to what eats the food: seed to mouse to hawk.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.C',3,'Which animal eats other animals?','["a rabbit", "a cow", "a hawk", "a deer"]'::jsonb,2,'A hawk eats mice and other small animals.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.C',2,'Which is the first link in most food chains?','["a frog", "a hawk", "a snake", "a plant"]'::jsonb,3,'Plants make food, so most food chains start with a plant.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.C',3,'A frog eats a fly. What would happen to the frog if there were no flies?','["it would have less food", "it would grow wings", "nothing would change", "it would have more food"]'::jsonb,0,'Animals depend on what they eat.','original'),
('112.3.b.12.C',4,'A cricket eats plants. A bird eats the cricket. Which does the bird depend on for food?','["the wind", "the small insect", "the soil only", "the rain only"]'::jsonb,1,'The bird gets its food from the cricket, which is a small insect.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.A',2,'A bird has wings. What can wings help many birds do?','["dig tunnels", "climb walls", "fly", "swim like a fish"]'::jsonb,2,'Wings help most birds fly.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.A',3,'A fish has fins and gills. What do fins help it do?','["run", "fly", "dig", "swim"]'::jsonb,3,'Fins help fish move in water.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.A',2,'Which animal has fur that keeps it warm?','["a bear", "a fish", "a frog", "a snake"]'::jsonb,0,'Fur keeps a bear warm.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.A',3,'A duck has webbed feet. What do they help it do?','["dig holes", "swim", "climb trees", "fly high"]'::jsonb,1,'Webbed feet push water to help a duck swim.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.A',3,'A turtle has a hard shell. What does the shell help it do?','["swim fast", "fly", "stay safe", "see in the dark"]'::jsonb,2,'A shell protects a turtle.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.A',2,'Which animal has a long neck that helps it reach leaves in tall trees?','["a rabbit", "a mouse", "a frog", "a giraffe"]'::jsonb,3,'A giraffe''s long neck helps it reach high leaves.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.A',4,'Why does a woodpecker have a strong, pointed beak?','["to peck into trees for food", "to make a nest of mud", "to run fast", "to swim"]'::jsonb,0,'A woodpecker''s beak is used to peck wood for insects.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.B',2,'A bird starts its life inside what?','["a cocoon", "an egg", "a pod", "a seed"]'::jsonb,1,'Birds hatch from eggs.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.B',3,'Which order shows a bird''s life cycle?','["adult bird, egg, chick", "egg, adult bird, chick", "egg, chick, adult bird", "chick, egg, adult bird"]'::jsonb,2,'A bird hatches from an egg as a chick, then grows into an adult.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.B',2,'Which is a mammal?','["a fish", "a frog", "a bird", "a dog"]'::jsonb,3,'A dog is a mammal.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.B',3,'How do baby mammals get their first food?','["they drink milk from their mother", "they eat seeds", "they catch fish", "they dig for roots"]'::jsonb,0,'Mammal mothers feed their babies milk.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.B',3,'A fish starts as an egg and hatches into a tiny fish. What comes next?','["it grows legs and walks", "it grows into an adult fish", "it becomes an egg again", "it turns into a bird"]'::jsonb,1,'A young fish grows into an adult fish.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.B',2,'A puppy grows up to be what?','["a bird", "a cat", "a dog", "a fish"]'::jsonb,2,'A puppy grows into an adult dog.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.B',4,'Which animal does NOT start life inside an egg?','["a robin", "a duck", "a trout", "a horse"]'::jsonb,3,'A horse is a mammal and the baby grows inside the mother.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.C',2,'A kitten looks most like which animal?','["a grown cat", "a grown dog", "a grown fish", "a grown frog"]'::jsonb,0,'Young animals look like their parents.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.C',2,'A baby duck has feathers, a beak, and webbed feet like its parents. What does this show?','["ducks do not grow", "young animals look like their parents", "ducks are plants", "all animals look the same"]'::jsonb,1,'Young animals resemble their parents.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.C',3,'A calf is a young cow. What does the calf have like its parents?','["a shell", "wings and feathers", "four legs and a tail", "fins and gills"]'::jsonb,2,'A calf looks like a small cow.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.C',3,'A puppy has ears and a tail like its mother. Which is the same?','["the size", "the age", "the weight", "the body parts"]'::jsonb,3,'The puppy has the same kinds of body parts as its mother.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.C',3,'A chick looks small. How is it like its parents?','["it has feathers and a beak", "it has fins", "it has a shell", "it has fur"]'::jsonb,0,'A chick has feathers and a beak like adult chickens.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.C',2,'A baby giraffe looks like which animal?','["a lion", "an adult giraffe", "a zebra", "an elephant"]'::jsonb,1,'A baby giraffe looks like an adult giraffe.','original'),
('112.3.b.13.C',4,'A student finds a baby animal with spots. The mother also has spots. What can the student say?','["young animals never look like parents", "all animals have spots", "young animals can look like their parents", "spots are rocks"]'::jsonb,2,'The baby and mother share the same pattern.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Science' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
